[metadata] {"type": "create", "filePath": "/workspace/repo/.changeset/switch-case-trailing-comment.md", "content": "---
"@biomejs/biome": patch
---

Fixed a formatter idempotence bug where a trailing line comment on a `switch` case clause was moved into a following block statement.

Previously, a trailing line comment on a case clause whose body was a single block statement was pushed after the opening brace, and reformatting the result moved it again onto its own line inside the block:

```diff
  switch (foo) {
    case 1: // comment 1
-   case 2: { // comment 2
+   case 2: // comment 2
+     {
        doStuff();
-   }
+     }
  }
```

Biome now keeps such comments on their original case line and breaks the block onto the next line, producing stable output across repeated formatting in both space and tab indentation modes.
